      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0e2a9997_315cd770",
        "filename": "zephyr/test/accel_cal/CMakeLists.txt",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 20,
      "author": {
        "id": 1331721
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-02T23:04:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e en just ticking the compiler version might break this.\nThat\u0027s a strong argument *for* Jack\u0027s suggestion of using a tolerance in the comparison.",
      "parentUuid": "dc12290f_227de02d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 20,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 20,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "be3836a30aa2813c88e726a682ad73d6ebbf07da",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9749d420_63245d60",
        "filename": "zephyr/test/accel_cal/CMakeLists.txt",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 20,
      "author": {
        "id": 1333748
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-02T23:42:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But if we use a tolerance and then tick the compiler, that uprev might push us out of the tolerance range. So we\u0027d have to hunt this down again. I don\u0027t want to start playing the game of \"well we just need to add X to the tolerance, that\u0027s still OK\". Well at what point do you know that you\u0027ve gone too far?\n\nHere we\u0027re compiling for a very specific arc which means that all builds will be the same.",
      "parentUuid": "0e2a9997_315cd770",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 20,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 20,
        "endChar": 69
      },
